/// The services the project needs to run locally, in compose.yaml for
/// Docker Compose: task up starts them and waits until they are ready, task
/// down stops them (docker compose down -v also deletes their data). Other
/// blueprints add their services. Everything is prefixed with name, the
/// app's by default: the Compose project, its containers (loja-postgres) and
/// volumes (loja-postgres-data), easy to tell apart in Docker.
blueprint compose {
  version "0.1.0"
  requires app

  /// Prefix of the Compose project, its containers and volumes; the app's
  /// name when empty. Change it when two of your apps share a name.
  option name string default("")
  /// Ports the services listen on locally, as "service:port", e.g.
  /// ["postgres:5433"] when another project already uses 5432.
  option ports list default([])

  /// Services of compose.yaml, indented by two spaces; a blank line goes
  /// between contributions. Give containers the prefix with container_name,
  /// and volumes with their name property (Compose would add the project
  /// otherwise); the prefix is or (index (optionsOf "compose") "name")
  /// .App.Kebab.
  slot "compose.services"
  /// Named volumes of compose.yaml, indented by two spaces, each with a
  /// name: property with the prefix.
  slot "compose.volumes"
}
